# UI Foundation Reset — UserXpert Design System (Highest Priority)

## IMPORTANT
From this point onward, **ignore all previous UI, styling, component, layout, animation, and design instructions** given in this project unless they are explicitly restated below.

Treat this document as the **single source of truth** for every UI decision.

If any previous prompt, memory, file, or instruction conflicts with this document:
- This document ALWAYS wins.
- Never fall back to older styling.
- Never mix multiple design systems.
- Never reuse previous visual decisions unless requested.

---

# Our Stack

Install and use:

- Radix UI
- Tailwind CSS
- Motion (Motion for React / Framer Motion)

Do NOT install or use:
- shadcn/ui
- Chakra UI
- Mantine
- Ant Design
- Bootstrap
- DaisyUI
- Any other component library unless explicitly requested.

---

# Design Philosophy

We DO NOT copy Google visually.

We ONLY follow Material Design 3 principles for:

- Accessibility
- Usability
- Form UX
- Layout logic
- Typography hierarchy
- States
- Interaction patterns
- Motion guidelines

Visual inspiration should instead feel closer to:

- Linear
- Vercel
- Stripe
- Raycast
- Apple

The result should feel:

- Modern
- Premium
- Minimal
- Futuristic
- Fast
- Trustworthy
- Human

Never look template-based.

---

# Accessibility (Mandatory)

Follow:

- Material Design 3
- WCAG 2.2 AA
- NN/g usability principles
- Baymard form UX research

Every component must include:

✓ keyboard navigation

✓ visible focus state

✓ screen reader support

✓ semantic HTML

✓ proper ARIA

✓ proper labels

✓ logical tab order

✓ accessible validation

✓ accessible error messages

✓ reduced motion support

✓ high color contrast

Accessibility is NOT optional.

---

# Forms

Forms are the highest priority of this project.

Requirements:

- large touch targets
- obvious labels
- helper text when needed
- inline validation
- instant feedback
- beautiful success states
- disabled/loading states
- keyboard friendly
- autofill support
- mobile friendly
- country selector UX
- never placeholder-only labels

Every form should feel effortless.

---

# Visual Style

Create a premium identity.

Use:

- generous whitespace
- rounded corners
- subtle shadows
- elegant gradients
- soft depth
- premium typography
- clean iconography
- tasteful animations

Avoid:

- glassmorphism everywhere
- neon overload
- huge borders
- noisy backgrounds
- excessive blur
- heavy gradients
- clutter

Less is more.

---

# Motion

Use Motion for:

- page transitions
- hover feedback
- button interactions
- cards
- dialogs
- accordions
- drawers
- modals
- form success
- loading

Animation rules:

- subtle
- smooth
- performant

Prefer:

150–250ms

Avoid flashy animations.

Animations should communicate, never distract.

---

# Typography

Base font:

16px

Minimum:

14px

Readable line heights.

Strong hierarchy.

Never tiny text.

Never cramped spacing.

---

# Layout

Always build using an 8px spacing system.

Maintain consistent rhythm.

Large breathing space.

Clear visual hierarchy.

Responsive first.

Mobile first.

---

# Components

Build custom branded components using Radix primitives.

Do NOT make components resemble default Radix demos.

Create a unique UserXpert identity.

Every reusable component should be:

- accessible
- reusable
- responsive
- composable
- polished

---

# Code Quality

Every component should be:

clean

modular

typed

reusable

maintainable

performant

accessible

---

# Decision Rule

Whenever you are uncertain between:

A) prettier

B) more usable

Always choose:

MORE USABLE.

---

# Persistence

Before generating any UI, silently verify:

- Am I following THIS document?
- Am I ignoring previous design instructions?
- Am I still using Radix + Tailwind + Motion?
- Am I following Material Design 3 principles instead of copying Material visuals?
- Is accessibility satisfied?
- Is this premium?
- Is this unique?
- Is this production-ready?

If the answer to any is NO,

stop,

correct the design,

then continue.

This document remains the permanent design authority for the project until explicitly replaced.